leakscan ports the default leak-detection patterns of IronClaw's leak detector to Go.

Upstream: https://github.com/nearai/ironclaw
File:     crates/substrates/ironclaw_safety/src/leak_detector.rs
          (exact-value redaction ideas from crates/substrates/ironclaw_safety/src/redaction.rs)
Commit:   b0b999d96781516ee05e6ba961d6f3ead900da96 (main, 2026-09-10)
License:  MIT OR Apache-2.0; this port uses it under the MIT license, reproduced below.

What was ported: the pattern regexes, severities and actions (21 of the 23 defaults; NEAR AI's session
pattern and IronClaw's sandbox-placeholder pattern are left out, per docs/21-gateway-v0.md), the bare-JWT
header check and its 64 KiB fail-closed bound, range merging for redaction, and test vectors. Everything
about decoding before scanning, exact-secret redaction across encodings and the streaming redactor is ours, as are
the patterns after upstream's (tacy_placeholder and the siblings added in VM release 2, from aws_temp_access_key on).

